                                "sense_id": "269696a1-481c-3014-9c6d-d3d91d6e7119",
                                "text": "There is a house in Cherry street, not far from Catherine Market […]. A little to the north of its door stands an old-time tree; and for many a year it has been known to the “crossmen” and “knucks” of the town as “Jack Circle's watering place” and “fence.”"
                            },
